                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4050e93-9d74-3685-a382-b5d0797021a7",
                        "entry_id": "73629b26-a298-3b83-a7e6-e9afb05f93b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "uczucie niepokoju, niepewności"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccd0a138-040a-4095-b9bc-2e8ae7f66a4f",
                                "sense_id": "e4050e93-9d74-3685-a382-b5d0797021a7",
                                "text": "Moskwa zaczęła również przejawiać coraz wyraźniejsze zaniepokojenie rosnącą obecnością amerykańską w regionie"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80a3c7da-4582-424d-bb82-cf2c3b72c73a",
                        "source_entry_id": "73629b26-a298-3b83-a7e6-e9afb05f93b7",
                        "source_sense_id": "e4050e93-9d74-3685-a382-b5d0797021a7",
                        "target_lang_word": "disquietude",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disquietude",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50478b45-3c7f-3b77-80b4-173a2053d54b",
                                        "entry_id": "3d97bb83-20fe-35db-a4a7-18d6b5e35675",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of disquiet, uneasiness, or anxiety."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd3f3ec8-2bec-48c1-89df-460744308d19",
                                                "sense_id": "50478b45-3c7f-3b77-80b4-173a2053d54b",
                                                "text": "One would think there should be something wonderfully pleasing in the Possession of Fame, that, notwithstanding all these mortifying Considerations, can engage a Man in so desperate a Pursuit; and yet if we consider the little Happiness that attends a great Character, and the Multitude of Disquietudes to which the Desire of it subjects an ambitious Mind, one would be still the more surprised to see so many restless Candidates for Glory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59d876d5-46d2-4b75-b85d-bea56d0f1dd6",
                                                "sense_id": "50478b45-3c7f-3b77-80b4-173a2053d54b",
                                                "text": "[…]but Mr Blifil said, he had received such positive and repeated orders from his uncle, never to keep any secret from him for fear of the disquietude which it might give him, that he durst not think of disobedience, whatever might be the consequence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4bb226a-8cf4-4885-a3e2-3bccf4936812",
                                                "sense_id": "50478b45-3c7f-3b77-80b4-173a2053d54b",
                                                "text": "He was at length called forth, and set apart by fasting and prayer to the ministerial office, which he executed with faithfulness and success during a long course of years; though frequently with the greatest trepidation and inward disquietude."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc3d9d8a-2635-4aca-9462-375de3b4370a",
                                                "sense_id": "50478b45-3c7f-3b77-80b4-173a2053d54b",
                                                "text": "For with Rosilia, to the regret of the past and self-accusation, was added the contemplation of a dark futurity, seldom affording a gleam of hope to cheer and solace her disquietude."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1250090-c464-3f11-990f-3dfda058239c",
                                        "entry_id": "3d97bb83-20fe-35db-a4a7-18d6b5e35675",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fear or an instance of uneasiness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9670486d-2eec-45db-ae35-8c36960c43a0",
                                                "sense_id": "c1250090-c464-3f11-990f-3dfda058239c",
                                                "text": "The cares and disquietudes of the marriage-state, quoth Mrs. Wadman, are very great."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "adb353f3-4e46-4c3e-88a3-0d802800042c",
                                                "sense_id": "c1250090-c464-3f11-990f-3dfda058239c",
                                                "text": "The lawyer stood awhile when Mr. Hyde had left him, the picture of disquietude."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07a4d10c-643d-4363-981d-bf9ba8173e00",
                        "source_entry_id": "73629b26-a298-3b83-a7e6-e9afb05f93b7",
                        "source_sense_id": "e4050e93-9d74-3685-a382-b5d0797021a7",
                        "target_lang_word": "disquiet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disquiet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33767861-b628-3dec-a85e-607543ecc7af",
                                        "entry_id": "5160facb-a5d6-339e-9476-8650f75e42de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lack of quiet; absence of tranquility in body or mind"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "107d1973-fe75-4da7-8736-c81ec60c3ca1",
                                                "sense_id": "33767861-b628-3dec-a85e-607543ecc7af",
                                                "text": "My journey had been my own suggestion, and Elizabeth therefore acquiesced, but she was filled with disquiet at the idea of my suffering, away from her, the inroads of misery and grief."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8ced2d1-c27f-4a32-a12b-3e57d4741267",
                                                "sense_id": "33767861-b628-3dec-a85e-607543ecc7af",
                                                "text": "Every house has its skeleton in it somewhere, and it may be a comfort to some unhappy folks to think that the luckier and most wealthy of their neighbours have their miseries and causes of disquiet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3741053-b44d-46ce-9981-0757051e2aee",
                                                "sense_id": "33767861-b628-3dec-a85e-607543ecc7af",
                                                "text": "I wish to say in regard to the alleged matter of disquiet in this Church, that when I received the postal card that was sent, I suppose, to all the clergy of the Church, I could not but feel in my heart that the three distinguished gentlemen who signed that postal card, or whose names were attached to it, and put it forth, were disquieting the Church much more than the Prayer-Book."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disquiet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25acb25f-cb46-305d-bc40-8776aaca3ba1",
                                        "entry_id": "e52a21a7-e803-37ba-99aa-80b071b066eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deprived of quiet; impatient, restless, uneasy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ece22eb-c6a8-483c-a81c-e800c747a585",
                                                "sense_id": "25acb25f-cb46-305d-bc40-8776aaca3ba1",
                                                "text": "I pray you huſband be not ſo diſquiet. / The meate was well, if you were ſo contented."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5abd2e37-c59e-4bd1-872c-de791f5a7d7a",
                                                "sense_id": "25acb25f-cb46-305d-bc40-8776aaca3ba1",
                                                "text": "How rare is it for men to get their lot in the world brought up to their deſire? but are ſtill at ſome jar with their preſent condition, ſo that oft there needs no more to turn men discontent but the thought of ſome lot, which they apprehend more ſatiſfying than their own, the want whereof turns them more diſquiet than all their enjoyments are pleaſing; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "101b4f4f-fe39-4ec8-a5c6-dd5c6ae3b72a",
                                                "sense_id": "25acb25f-cb46-305d-bc40-8776aaca3ba1",
                                                "text": "From this place it was that i uſed to go often to view my boat; and now i ſhall relate a thing that gave me the moſt diſquiet of any thing i had ever met with, ſince my firſt coming into the iſland. […] [O]ne day, as i was going to my boat, as uſual, i perceived on the ſand, the print of a man's naked foot, and had i ſeen an apparition, i could not have been more terrified."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e65e5b0a-d61e-4ec6-9684-da50547d4366",
                                                "sense_id": "25acb25f-cb46-305d-bc40-8776aaca3ba1",
                                                "text": "My vina breaks out in a strange disquiet measure, / My heart to-day is tremulous with the heart-throbs of the world."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disquiet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52900d29-cd4b-32da-91cf-5229cfd6ab31",
                                        "entry_id": "fd86e97b-e492-3d18-98d7-e0c7758e0775",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (someone or something) worried or anxious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "530c7580-65af-46a9-81ea-785851a3094a",
                                                "sense_id": "52900d29-cd4b-32da-91cf-5229cfd6ab31",
                                                "text": "He felt disquieted by the lack of interest the child had shown."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95a49451-d902-48af-930c-f99f2d28d825",
                                                "sense_id": "52900d29-cd4b-32da-91cf-5229cfd6ab31",
                                                "text": "They have been brought up religiouſly, and have been accuſtomed to read, and pray; and if at any time they do neglect and omit these duties, conſcience is upon them and upbraids and diſquiets them; and they are afraid to neglect them, leſt conſcience will queſtion and trouble them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "626e51c1-88f6-4dae-b2d9-bb09dd5f756f",
                                                "sense_id": "52900d29-cd4b-32da-91cf-5229cfd6ab31",
                                                "text": "This Bill, for taking away the Bishops Votes out of the Houſe of Peers, produced another Diſcovery, which caſt the Conductors farther behind, than they were Advanced by their Conqueſt amongst the Commons; and diſquieted them much more, than the other had Exalted them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "837c72ab-2e16-41a8-a46c-a3f9336ec596",
                                                "sense_id": "52900d29-cd4b-32da-91cf-5229cfd6ab31",
                                                "text": "Diſturbed and disquieted them, and made them very uneaſy; he terrified and distreſſed them; […] [Commentary on 1 Samuel 14:47.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56d9a49d-4f8f-4d53-a831-ea71cebb8c4c",
                                                "sense_id": "52900d29-cd4b-32da-91cf-5229cfd6ab31",
                                                "text": "She had had a wonderful interview respecting Fanny on this very day, and was at this moment disquieting her mind because she could not tell her friend what had happened without a breach of confidence!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "214b9070-35a5-4bac-998d-e8af9e0cd5ca",
                                                "sense_id": "52900d29-cd4b-32da-91cf-5229cfd6ab31",
                                                "text": "I wish to say in regard to the alleged matter of disquiet in this Church, that when I received the postal card that was sent, I suppose, to all the clergy of the Church, I could not but feel in my heart that the three distinguished gentlemen who signed that postal card, or whose names were attached to it, and put it forth, were disquieting the Church much more than the Prayer-Book."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "603c0323-544d-4c40-a731-98cfcf5758e2",
                                                "sense_id": "52900d29-cd4b-32da-91cf-5229cfd6ab31",
                                                "text": "What disquieted the Christian friends was not that this was an awful state of affairs theologically. What disquieted them the most was the fact that they were disquieted. As liberal-minded adults they had not expected to be disturbed at all."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
